==== hyperbricks yaml {!{page}} ====
page:
  - type: hypermedia
  - route: nested-tree-3-level

  - content:
      - type: tree

      - section_block:
          - type: tree

          - article_block:
              - type: tree

              - title:
                  - type: html
                  - value: |
                      <h1>Three level tree</h1>

              - body:
                  - type: text
                  - value: Tree level three keeps leaf order.
==== explainer ====
Three nested TREE components keep source order without numeric child keys.
The {!{page}} reference in the header selects the root object that is materialized and rendered.
==== expected json ====
{
  "@order": [
    "content"
  ],
  "@type": "<HYPERMEDIA>",
  "content": {
    "@order": [
      "section_block"
    ],
    "@type": "<TREE>",
    "section_block": {
      "@order": [
        "article_block"
      ],
      "@type": "<TREE>",
      "article_block": {
        "@order": [
          "title",
          "body"
        ],
        "@type": "<TREE>",
        "body": {
          "@type": "<TEXT>",
          "value": "Tree level three keeps leaf order."
        },
        "title": {
          "@type": "<HTML>",
          "value": "<h1>Three level tree</h1>\n"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "route": "nested-tree-3-level"
}
==== expected output ====
<!DOCTYPE html><html><body><h1>Three level tree</h1>
Tree level three keeps leaf order.</body></html>
